RECENT CONVERSATION

The following dialogue represents recent conversational context.

Use it only to maintain natural continuity.

Remember:
- what was just said
- who said it
- the current conversational topic
- unanswered questions
- recent emotional tone

Do not repeat information that was already established.

Do not restart a topic that has naturally ended.

Do not force continuation of the previous topic when the current scene has moved on.

If the current activity, location, participants, or situation has changed, allow the old conversation to end naturally.

Recent dialogue is context, not a script.

Characters may change the subject, become silent, or return attention to their own activities.
